---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import Portrait from '@/components/Portrait.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Bodhi McNally: a University of Sydney medical student with a background in data science, healthcare analytics and university teaching."
  ogType="profile"
>
  <PageHeader title="About" />

  <section class="about-opening container" aria-label="Professional biography">
    <aside class="about-sidebar">
      <Portrait variant="about" />

      <section class="appearances" aria-labelledby="appearances-title">
        <h2 id="appearances-title">I’ll be here…</h2>
        <ul>
          {
            site.appearances.map((appearance) => (
              <li>
                <time datetime={String(appearance.year)}>{appearance.year}</time>
                <div>
                  <p>{appearance.event}</p>
                  <span>{appearance.location}</span>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </section>
    </aside>

    <div class="about-narrative">
      <p>
        I am a Doctor of Medicine student at the University of Sydney, based at Westmead Clinical School. Before commencing medicine, I completed a Bachelor of Science at the University of Sydney with majors in Data Science and Genetics & Genomics.
      </p>

      <p>
        My quantitative background preceded medicine. Prior to commencing the MD, I worked at AstraZeneca applying statistical and computational methods to real-world healthcare data across multiple therapeutic areas. The work gave me practical experience with the strengths and limitations of routinely collected health data and reinforced the importance of understanding how data are generated before deciding how they should be analysed.
      </p>

      <p>
        I now want to apply that background to clinically useful questions in surgery. My developing research interests are focused on urology, particularly urological oncology, robotic and minimally invasive surgery, perioperative and functional outcomes, patient-reported outcomes, clinical prediction and the use of real-world clinical data. I hope to pursue a future career as an academic surgeon.
      </p>

      <p>
        Alongside medicine, I work as a Casual Academic in the University of Sydney’s School of Mathematics and Statistics, teaching undergraduate data science and statistics. Teaching remains an important part of my academic work and has led to broader interests in curriculum development, educational scholarship and Students-as-Partners initiatives.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am also a Surgical Research Scholar with RISE, where I have been matched to a surgical mentor and a research project aligned with urology. Over time, I would like to help strengthen pathways into research during medical school and the prevocational years, giving students and junior doctors opportunities to contribute meaningfully while developing the skills needed for academic practice.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="document-section" id="curriculum-vitae" aria-labelledby="cv-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="document-panel">
        <div>
          <h2 id="cv-title">Curriculum vitae</h2>
          <p>My current academic CV, updated {site.cv.updated}.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="document-panel__links">
          <a class="button" href={site.cv.driveHref} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
            View on Google Drive
          </a>
          <a class="text-link" href={site.cv.downloadHref} download>Download PDF</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cv-embed">
        <iframe
          src={`${site.cv.downloadHref}#view=FitH`}
          title="Bodhi McNally curriculum vitae"
          loading="lazy"
        ></iframe>
        <p>
          If the document does not appear in your browser, use the Google Drive or download links above.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
